  "Movies_and_TV:training_endpoint_interventions": "Fixed positive/negative endpoint pair, largest nonzero index, descriptive loader-row margin changes; rows are not identified independent users.",
  "Movies_and_TV:user_score_sensitivity": "Identified public training users, fixed 99 training-observed unseen candidates per user. Mean absolute score change and signed mean score change; no relevance labels, HR or target ranks.",
  "Movies_and_TV:temporal_geometry": "Identified-user strengths 0.25 and 0.5 use k=max(1,floor(fraction*original_nonpadding_length)), before baseline truncation. Interventions are unavailable when retained history cannot support the requested size or preserve the newest k items. Loader-row probes use their observed nonpadding lengths because full histories are unidentified. Deletions compact and left-pad; replacements preserve positions; shuffles preserve identities and multiplicities. Unchanged draws are excluded and counted, so shuffle estimates condition on changed draws.",
  "Movies_and_TV:user_intervals": "Pointwise 95% percentile intervals from 2000 seed-42 user bootstrap resamples. Each complete paired vector is resampled together within the current category and original-length stratum. Conditional on fitted model, fixed users/candidates; excludes training-seed, candidate-sampling and adaptive-search uncertainty. Exploratory, no p-values.",
  "Movies_and_TV:missingness": "Unavailable observations are null with reasons, never zero-effect evidence. Cross-category macro estimates require all four categories.",
  "Movies_and_TV:intact_user_endpoint_representations": "Raw and unit-normalized covariance statistics and norm quantiles for one intact final-nonpadding feature per identified training user eligible for the fixed-candidate sensitivity probe. Loader endpoint statistics remain separate and may contain repeated users.",
  "Movies_and_TV:paired_contrasts": "Within-user difference between each named method and the first method in its declared comparison family, computed on common eligible users. Bootstrap intervals resample each complete paired vector together. These are score-sensitivity contrasts, not ranking improvements.",
